     "result_text_tail": "failure is why the recommendation adds the redesign and the bundle-delivery fix.\n\n**Calls I made since you weren't available** (all listed on slide 19; please check them with Finance and Operations):\n- The exit takes effect on 1 July 2027.\n- The $2.1M penalty counts against the $0.9M cash limit.\n- The 25% migration to D is treated as a ceiling, not a forecast.\n- The $2.9M of leftover shared cost is split across A, B and D in proportion to what they carry today.\n- The redesign runs March\u2013August 2027, with savings starting in September.\n- Figures cover 2027\u201329 and are not discounted.\n\n**Not in the briefing pack:**\n- The cost of losing the engineering team for four months isn't quantified. I show only a labelled upper estimate of about $0.25M, under a stated assumption.\n- The Q3 2027 target for getting bundle delivery back to 95%, and the proposed owners for each workstream, are mine for management to confirm.\n\n**About the files:** this sandbox has no PowerPoint renderer, so the PDF is my own preview drawn with Arial, and fonts may differ slightly from PowerPoint. I checked every slide visually and the file reopens cleanly, but I haven't opened it in PowerPoint. All shapes and text are editable; the charts are drawn from shapes rather than built-in PowerPoint chart objects.\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/` (the script that rebuilds the deck is `./work/build_deck.py`):\n- `Vesper_MedTech_Connector_C_Board_Deck.pptx`\n- `Vesper_MedTech_Connector_C_Board_Deck_preview.pdf`\n- `README.md`"
